From 3dbd5428ffb8bb5d9aac78d653f36e346614ce98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci(review-comment): refresh the PR's bot comment
 when CI completes on its wt/ head

hermes-core-wt ship lands a PR only once the ci-review-bot comment says
"ran on <exact head>". The bot ran only hourly (cron :17) or on a manual
dispatch, and every ship rebase makes a new head, so an approved,
CI-green PR waited up to an hour after each rebase. PR1104 (2026-11-12):
"All required checks pass (v2)" green 10:42:31Z, exact-head review 10:43Z,
ship refused twice with rc 3 until a hand dispatch at 10:52Z; four of the
six bot runs 09:21-10:52Z were hand dispatches working around the lag.

Add a workflow_run trigger on CI completed for wt/** branches (what ship
pushes). The job runs only for same-repo pull_request CI runs that ended
success/failure, and passes the run's head sha as TARGET_HEAD_SHA;
batch_review_comments.py --head-sha then refreshes only the open PR at
that exact head, so no other PR's comment is rewritten. On PR heads the
sibling Docker run finishes before CI (60/60 sampled wt/ heads, 5-36 min
earlier), so this single run posts the final "ran on" comment. Targeted
runs get a concurrency group per head: a shared group keeps one pending
run and cancels the rest. The hourly sweep and workflow_dispatch stay.
The checkout stays on the default branch; only a validated 40-hex sha
crosses from the event.

Proof: tests/ci/test_batch_review_comments.py, 10 new/changed cases fail
on 0edc432d7d (workflow shape, targeted refresh names the new head,
no-match no-op, env wiring, non-sha refusal) and pass here; 79 tests in
the batch/live-comment/runner-routing files pass; actionlint 1.7.12 (the
pinned version) clean on all workflows.
